# build-with-tests

Follow every step in order. Don't start a step until the previous one is done.

## 1. Read before touching anything
- [ ] `CLAUDE.md` and `.claude/stagegate/stack.md`
- [ ] The approved brief, if there is one: stay inside its scope
- [ ] 2–3 existing similar features; note the patterns to copy
- [ ] If a documentation tool is available (e.g. Context7), current docs for each library you'll use

## 2. Branch
`git branch --show-current` must not be `{{ project.default_branch }}`. Otherwise
`git switch -c {{ git.branch_prefix }}<slug>`.

## 3. Smallest coherent steps
For each unit (a type/schema, a function, an entry point{{#if stack.frontend_dir}}, a component, an API client call{{/if}}):
1. Write the code.
2. Write its test immediately: success, failure, and empty/not-found paths. Mock every external service.
3. Run `{{ cmd.test }}` and make it pass.
4. Commit ({{#if git.per_file}}one file per commit{{else}}the unit and its test together{{/if}}).
Only then start the next unit.

## 4. Final verification
- [ ] `{{ cmd.test }}`: all green, no skipped or weakened tests
- [ ] `{{ cmd.lint }}`: clean
- [ ] `git diff --name-only {{ project.default_branch }}...HEAD`: only intended files
- [ ] Push the feature branch: `git push -u origin HEAD` (never `{{ project.default_branch }}`)

## 5. Summary
Files changed · patterns reused · new settings/env keys · test results · suggested CLAUDE.md additions.

## Rules
- No refactoring outside the scope; no new dependencies without the human's approval.
- If a test can't pass without breaking a CLAUDE.md rule, stop and report the conflict.
- Never commit secrets, state files or keys (the commit guard blocks them anyway).
